<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:trl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Trials;assembly=OpenRigs.Trials"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:gl="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Shaders;assembly=Bonsai.Shaders"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:task="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenDomeDecisionMakingTask;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig, which publishes it to every device piece; the launch's own, which rig-control always sets to C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs. ExperimentRecords and LiveView are not mapped from here: each reads that root as its own ConfigRoot, as a mapping edge into LiveView's StreamDevices would build it before the devices it streams." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" Description="The mouse's lab ID; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="SessionId" Description="The session number; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-localization.yml." />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561: SubjectId (the mouse's lab ID, or test), SessionId and LaunchId (the launcher's run id, which the manifest records) are the launch's; the experiment declares no parameter of its own: the task's own settings are the task file's, which rig-control writes at launch and again at Go with the form's edits, and names in TaskPath, its curriculum the only record of the stage; the pieces declare their own parameters and commands.The workflow starts into ready mode (devices connected, spouts homed and at this mouse's positions, live view on, nothing recorded) and reports Ready from Hardware. LaunchSettings (OpenRigs.Control) publishes SubjectId and TaskPath at Start and ExperimentIds (SubjectId, SessionId) at Go. TaskFile publishes the stage as TrainingCodeVersion (code-version, like S03A-k7f2, from the task file's curriculum) at Go and reports it as the metric trainingStage. SpoutStepSize and the spout commands are DomeHardware's LickSpoutStage's, which takes the step size live and shows its default. RewardValve-Left.Reward and RewardValve-Right.Reward each give 2.5 ul before and during a run through the valve's calibration (each RewardValve piece's manual drop, a fixed drop).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters />
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-localization.yml." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:LaunchSettings.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <TaskPath>..\config\task-localization.yml</TaskPath>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="1" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskFile</Name>
        <Description>Reads the task file (TaskPath) at Start into LaunchTaskConfig, as rig-control wrote it at launch, for the background noise, which plays from Ready; and at Go, with the form's edits, into TaskText (the file's text) and TaskConfig, each read by ReadTask, which keeps a trial condition's set values as numbers and bools. BackgroundNoise stops the workflow at Go if backgroundNoise was changed after launch, as the noise already plays at the launch's level. At Go, CheckTaskAtGo builds the trial conditions from TaskText (each condition's set over the task's values), checks the task once and publishes the trials' rules (TrialRules) for TaskLogic.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskPath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskText</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ReadTask" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskPath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ReadTask" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskText</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>CheckTaskAtGo</Name>
              <Description>The task file's text checked once, at Go, and the trials' rules built from it (TrialRules, tested C#): the task file's curriculum present and well formed, each trial condition built (its set and pairs over the task's values, every combination), rig.yml's speakers and Zapit's triggering, the draw's rules (TrialDraw.CheckTask: a stage past the table, the x-rules, a go/no-go task with no go trials, both spouts in go/no-go, a laser that would outlast the next trigger, ...) and with optogenetics the Zapit conditions file. A problem stops the workflow here, naming each, before the first trial.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CheckTaskAtGo" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TrainingCodeVersion</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrainingCodeVersion</Name>
              <Description>The stage as code-version (S03A-k7f2) from the task file's curriculum, found well formed by CheckTaskAtGo.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trainingStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Declarations</Name>
        <Description>Subjects the groups share. TrialEvents, the trial loop's events (RunTrials); Trial, each trial at its start; TrialRow, each trial's WorkflowData_Trials row, built at its outcome; GratingAzimuthDeg, the response; VisualStimulus, VisualStimulusOff and AuditoryStimulus, the stimuli. Zapit's commands and replies are ConnectForTask's, RewardRequests Rewards'.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>Trial</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="trl:TrialEvent(ext:Trial,ext:DecisionUpdate,ext:TrialOutcome)">
              <rx:Name>TrialEvents</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:TrialRow)">
              <rx:Name>TrialRow</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>VisualStimulus</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>VisualStimulusOff</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>AuditoryStimulus</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentLogs.bonsai">
        <Description>The experiment folder at Go (PathPrefix), WorkflowData_Events, Settings_Rig, Settings_Experiment and the Recording phase. Before Hardware: every device's log waits for PathPrefix, so its definition must read nothing the devices define.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (DomeHardware's ProjectorDisplay); a launch property." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The dome's devices (OpenRigs.Devices DomeHardware: every device as a piece, each logging itself; the cameras triggered once all three acquire; the speakers and their mixer; the projector, DisplayDevice a launch property), with Ready once the Harp clock is set, the spouts are homed, each camera has sent a frame and the mixer has started, and a stop naming what never came after 180 s.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:DomeHardware.bonsai">
              <Description>Every dome device as a piece, named as in the data (lib-open-rigs Building Blocks): the Ready gate, the timestamp generator's clock, the Behavior board with its reward lines, Zapit line and wheel, both Lickety Splits, the lick spout stage, the three cameras, which start triggering once all three acquire, the speakers (SpeakerMixer) and the projector (ProjectorDisplay, stimuli on DrawStimuli).</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="0" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Display</Name>
        <Description>Each trial's grating, drawn on DomeHardware's projector (DrawStimuli).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>VisualStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ShowGrating</Name>
              <Description>Draws a trial's grating from VisualStimulus until VisualStimulusOff: contrast, elevation and phase the trial's, the rest the task's, the azimuth the trial's, then GratingAzimuthDeg's as the licks move it (so its first frame is never the last trial's), flickering at the stimulus set's pulse rate, with the photodiode square black on its on frames and white on its off frames.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>Flicker</Name>
                    <Description>The grating on and off at the auditory stimulus set's pulse rate (AuditoryStimulusSet.PulseRateHz): each half period is its FlickerHalfPeriod, mapped in. A render-clock stimulus, not a task wait.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="gl:Timer">
                      <gl:DueTime>PT0S</gl:DueTime>
                      <gl:Period>PT0S</gl:Period>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Mod">
                    <Operand xsi:type="WorkflowProperty" TypeArguments="sys:Int64">
                      <Value>2</Value>
                    </Operand>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>On?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>Item2 == 0</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>Off?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>Item2 != 0</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Contrast" Selector="visualContrast" />
                      <Property Name="LocationY" Selector="visualElevationDeg" />
                      <Property Name="Phase" Selector="visualPhaseRad" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="TemporalFrequency" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.TemporalFrequencyHz" />
                      <Property Name="SpatialFrequency" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.SpatialFrequencyCpd" />
                      <Property Name="Angle" Selector="TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.OrientationDeg" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Aperture" Selector="it" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>Aperture</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The Gaussian window's sigma relative to the grating's 100 degree extent.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>TaskParameters.VisualStimulus.GaussianWindowSigmaDeg * 2 / 100.0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="LocationX" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawGratings.bonsai">
                    <LocationX>0</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>0</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <ExtentX>100</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>100</ExtentY>
                    <SpatialFrequency>0.06666667</SpatialFrequency>
                    <TemporalFrequency>0</TemporalFrequency>
                    <Phase>0</Phase>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <SquareWave>false</SquareWave>
                    <Contrast>0</Contrast>
                    <DutyCycle xsi:nil="true" />
                    <Radius>1</Radius>
                    <Aperture>0.4</Aperture>
                    <Opacity>1</Opacity>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualStimulusOff</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>0</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>0</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>0</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>1</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>1</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>1</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:IgnoreElements" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Period" Selector="FlickerHalfPeriod" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>visualAzimuthDeg</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="33" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="33" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="20" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="20" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="20" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="20" Label="Source5" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="22" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="25" To="24" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="24" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="27" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="27" To="26" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="26" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="28" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="30" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Audio</Name>
        <Description>The sounds, played by DomeHardware's speakers and mixer (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: Speakers, and the mixer started no sooner than 3 s after Start, never sooner, as a fault while the sound card boots can blue-screen the PC); each trial's sound at its auditoryAmplitude (1 the waveform as stored), TaskLogic's penalty sound at penalty.sound.levelDbfs, checked when the task file is read at Go; the background noise at the launch's task file's level, checked at Start and sent at Ready. The auditory stimulus set equalised for rig.yml's speakers at Start (LoadAuditoryStimulusSet), then at Go for the largest amplitude any condition can draw (TrialRules.Loudest into LevelAuditoryStimulusSet, which stops the workflow, naming the condition and speaker, if any would peak at -1 dBFS after equalisation); the lab's penalty sound (PlayPenaltySound, in TaskLogic) on penaltySoundChannel at penalty.sound.levelDbfs. The background noise is the BackgroundNoise include's, after this group.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:LoadAuditoryStimulusSet">
                <ext:Folder>sounds</ext:Folder>
                <ext:FilePrefix>filtered_pink_pulse_train_</ext:FilePrefix>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>AuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Loudest</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:LevelAuditoryStimulusSet" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>LevelledAuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>AuditoryStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>AuditoryTrial?</Name>
              <Description>A trial at auditoryStimulus.amplitude 0 plays no sound.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>auditoryOn</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>PlayAuditoryStimulus</Name>
              <Description>Plays a trial's sound: its waveform equalised for its speaker (the channel of rig.yml's speaker nearest the drawn location), scaled by its auditoryAmplitude, with the sync copy on rig.yml's syncChannel at syncGain.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>LevelledAuditoryStimulusSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>AuditoryTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="ext:SelectAuditoryStimulus" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusSounds</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:IgnoreElements" />
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:BackgroundNoise.bonsai">
        <Description>The background noise, the lab's one file, rig.yml's speakerArray.backgroundNoise (60 s of white noise, 32-bit float), unequalised on every speaker at the launched task file's backgroundNoise.levelDbfs from Ready; Go stops if the task file changed backgroundNoise after launch.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ConnectForTask.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Everything else written to the experiment folder (ExperimentLogs, before Hardware, makes it at Go, with WorkflowData_Events, Settings_Rig and Settings_Experiment; each device logs itself): TaskLogs (OpenRigs.Logging) writes Settings_Task (the task file as JSON), WorkflowData_Trials and Zapit's logs (each reply an Events row, ZapitReply, and Settings_ZapitConditions); Rewards (OpenRigs.Devices) logs each reward (RewardDelivered) and each RewardValve piece its calibration file (a valve with no calibration stops the workflow, for every mouse); ExperimentRecords, last but LiveView, adds the controller's events to WorkflowData_Events, records the Harp devices and writes the manifest.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="task:SerializeToJson">
                <task:Formatting>Indented</task:Formatting>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:TaskLogs.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Status</Name>
        <Description>The current trial's facts as metrics, named as WorkflowData_Trials's columns (trialNumber, target, trialType, visualAzimuthDeg, auditoryAzimuthDeg, rewardOfferedUl, laserCondition; the trainingStage, code-version, is TaskFile's); rig-control computes counts, water and performance from the files.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>trialNumber</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialNumber</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>target</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>target</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>trialType</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialType</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>visualAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>visualAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>auditoryAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>auditoryAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>rewardOfferedUl</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>rewardOfferedUl</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>laserCondition</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>laserCondition</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Rewards.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RewardValve.bonsai">
        <Name>RewardValve-Left</Name>
        <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
        <BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RewardValve.bonsai">
        <Name>RewardValve-Right</Name>
        <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
        <BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The trials, every time on the Harp clock: TrialRules (checked and built at Go, TaskFile's CheckTaskAtGo) run by lib-open-rigs' TrialLoop (RunTrials) into TrialEvents once the experiment folder exists, the first trial's interval starting then; each kind picked from them (PickTrialEvents) and sent to the hardware. Start: Trial (Status) and the seed; Arm and Trigger: Zapit's StartStimulus (Zapit) and the ZapitTrigger line raised, cleared at TriggerOff; Stimulus: the grating and the sound; Update: the decision variable and the grating's azimuth; the cues GratingOff (stimulusSeconds after the stimulus), SpoutsIn (stimulusToSpoutsInSeconds after it) and Drink (drinkSeconds into the next interval, with spout movements: the spouts out); Outcome: the trial's row (TrialRow), the reward (RewardRequests), the spouts and the penalty sound. Zapit adds no time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>OnNextTick</Name>
              <Description>The rules, once the experiment folder exists, stamped with the next Harp clock tick and given from the clock's thread (lib-open-rigs' OpenRigs.Core OnNextTick): the first trial's interval starts then.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:OnNextTick" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Value</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>WheelDistanceCm</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateLeft</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateRight</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitReplies</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>RunTrials</Name>
              <Description>The trials (TrialRules, tested C#, run by lib-open-rigs' TrialLoop) on the Harp clock: each drawn at its interval's start (the last outcome plus its timeout), started at the interval's end less the lead (max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0)) or later until the quiet waits hold (both spouts released for lickQuietSeconds; the wheel within wheelQuietCm over the last wheelQuietSeconds), the stimulus the lead after the start in every experiment, the response window responseDelaySeconds after it for responseWindowSeconds (each lick 1 left or -1 right on the decision variable, the grating moved degreesPerLick a lick; Left at thresholdLicks, Right at -thresholdLicks, else NoResponse at the window's end), the outcome, its timeout; with optogenetics each trial armed (Arm), triggered laserToStimulusSeconds before the stimulus unless answered first, and its line cleared laserDurationSeconds later (TriggerOff), the next armed once the longest ramp-down has played. Inputs: the rules, the clock, the wheel, the left and right lick states, Zapit's replies.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:RunTrials" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Start</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>rngSeed</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogRngSeed.bonsai">
              <Description>The seed every draw of the experiment follows from (the task file's rngSeed, or one drawn at Go when it is null), logged once at trial 1's start.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Optogenetics?</Name>
              <Description>An optogenetics experiment: the rules have a laser (optogenetics.enabled).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Laser != null</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>Zapit</Name>
              <Description>Once at Go, in an optogenetics experiment: ArmZapit given rig.yml's triggering and the task's laserDurationSeconds, which it reads as it starts (so here, after Go, not at Start), then sent each trial's StartStimulus. TrialLoop checks each reply (ZapitTrial.CheckArmed) and stops the workflow if Zapit has not armed a hardware-triggered trial by its trigger.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                      <trl:Kind>Arm</trl:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                      <trl:Kind>Trigger</trl:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="HardwareTriggered" Selector="Zapit.HardwareTriggered" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="DurationSeconds" Selector="TaskParameters.Optogenetics.LaserDurationSeconds" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>ArmZapit</Name>
                    <Description>Each laser trial's StartStimulus (its condition, laser on with the task's power or off at 0 mW, timed for laserDurationSeconds). On a hardware-triggered rig (rig.yml's zapit.hardwareTriggered) sent at Arm, during the interval; without, Zapit starts the laser on receipt, so it is sent at the Trigger.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:ZapitTrialCommand">
                      <trl:HardwareTriggered>false</trl:HardwareTriggered>
                      <trl:DurationSeconds>0</trl:DurationSeconds>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="11" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="11" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Trigger</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
              <Set>true</Set>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>TriggerOff</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
              <Set>false</Set>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Stimulus</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>VisualStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>AuditoryStimulus</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Update</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Update.GratingAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Cue</trl:Kind>
                <trl:Cue>GratingOff</trl:Cue>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>VisualStimulusOff</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Cue</trl:Kind>
                <trl:Cue>SpoutsIn</trl:Cue>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:SpoutsInCommand" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LickSpoutStage.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Cue</trl:Kind>
                <trl:Cue>Drink</trl:Cue>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:ToLickSpoutCommand">
                <dev:Command>SpoutsOut</dev:Command>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LickSpoutStage.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Outcome</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Outcome</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Row</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialRow</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Rewarded?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Rewarded</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Reward</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>SpoutMovementsAtOutcome?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>SpoutMovements</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SpoutCommand</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LickSpoutStage.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>PenaltySoundOn?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>PenaltySoundOn</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:PlayPenaltySound.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>SpoutMovements?</Name>
              <Description>Trial 1 starts with the spouts out, as every later trial does after the last one's drink; a task without spout movements (habituation) keeps them in.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item2.TaskParameters.SpoutMovements</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:ToLickSpoutCommand">
                <dev:Command>SpoutsOut</dev:Command>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LickSpoutStage.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="12" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="12" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="9" To="12" Label="Source4" />
            <Edge From="10" To="12" Label="Source5" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source6" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="36" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="38" To="39" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="39" To="40" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="40" To="41" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="43" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="43" To="44" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="44" To="45" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="45" To="46" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="47" To="48" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="48" To="49" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="49" To="50" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="51" To="52" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="52" To="53" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="53" To="54" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="54" To="55" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="53" To="56" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="56" To="57" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="57" To="58" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="53" To="59" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="59" To="60" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="60" To="61" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="53" To="62" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="62" To="63" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="64" To="65" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="65" To="67" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="66" To="67" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="67" To="68" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="68" To="69" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="69" To="70" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentRecords.bonsai">
        <Description>The controller's events (LogControlEvents), every Harp device in rig.yml checked at Start and recorded (RecordHarpDevices: the Behavior board, the timestamp generator, both stepper drivers and both Lickety Splits), and manifest.json (ExperimentManifest: the machine, this repo's commit, who launched it and sent Go, rig.yml and every file it names by hash ({RigFiles}: Projector-Mesh.csv, Projector-Gamma.bmp, the speakers' filters, the valve calibrations; the auditory stimuli are this repo's, in src\sounds, so the commit names them) and this mouse's spout positions, schemas\trial-columns.yml, and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml, the Harp device records (harp), the three settings files and WorkflowData (Trials and Events), Settings_ZapitConditions in an optogenetics experiment). Last but LiveView, as it finds each device by the subjects published before it.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
        <IngestScript>coen-dome-decision-making</IngestScript>
        <ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Task_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;WorkflowData/WorkflowData_Trials_;WorkflowData/WorkflowData_Events_;Settings/Settings_ZapitConditions_?Optogenetics</ExpectedFiles>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, from Start, in ready mode too. The three cameras as Camera-Face/Pupil/Body.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240, and the Behavior board's encoder from BehaviorBoard-Main.Data, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder appeared, and liveview, this workflow and its commit. Every message carries the rig and the session key, ready until the experiment folder exists. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use stops the workflow at Start.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
